  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">ZOA &amp; YMCA - Community-based sociotherapy, Liberia 2021-2022</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ZOA &amp; YMCA Community-based sociotherapy, Liberia 2021-2022 - ZOA &amp; YMCA Liberia 2021-2022</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Svenska ambassaden har f&#xe5;tt en f&#xf6;rfr&#xe5;gan av ZOA och YMCA att finansiera projektet &quot;Peacebuilding and Reconciliation through Community Dialogues II&quot; i Liberia med 11 600 000  kronor under perioden 2021-2022.

Huvudsyftet med st&#xf6;det &#xe4;r st&#xe4;rka konfliktl&#xf6;sning och f&#xf6;rsoning p&#xe5; lokal niv&#xe5;, samt att f&#xf6;rb&#xe4;ttra individers psykosociala v&#xe4;lm&#xe5;ende och familjedynamik och att st&#xe4;rka j&#xe4;mst&#xe4;lldhet p&#xe5; familjeniv&#xe5;.
Insatsen omfattar dessa omr&#xe5;den:

* F&#xf6;rb&#xe4;ttrad mental h&#xe4;lsa och psykosocialt v&#xe4;lm&#xe5;ende

* F&#xf6;rb&#xe4;ttrad social sammanh&#xe5;llning och medborgerligt f&#xf6;rtroende

* God sammh&#xe4;llsstyrning/good governance

* St&#xe4;rkt medborgardeltagande

* &#xd6;kad tillg&#xe5;ng till information</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ZOA and YMCA have applied to the Swedish Embassy for funding of 11 600 000 SEK to carry out the project &quot;Peacebuilding and Reconciliation through Community Dialogues II&quot; in Liberia during the period 2021-2022.

The intervention aims at strengthening conflict resolution and reconciliation initiatives at community and county level, while improving individual well-being and family dynamics, including more gender equal relations at the household level. The project is centered around these areas:

* Improved mental health and psychosocial well-being
* Improved co-existence and civic trust
* Good governance
* Increased levels of civic engagement
* Increased access to information

*Outcome 1: Improved psychosocial well-being and enhanced interpersonal relations within families and the community

*Outcome 2: Local leaders and government officials adhere to and act upon good governance principles

*Outcome 3: Improved civic participation and positive engagement with local government

*Outcome 4: A peaceful and safe school environment is established for students to reach their full potential

Outcome 5: Increased capacity of YMCA to independently implement similar projects</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overall objective of the project is to strengthen conflict resolution and reconciliation at community and county levels in Liberia. Through the implementation of community-based, bottom-up approaches in which project participants increase their self-awareness, learn more positive behaviours and are able to meaningfully connect to each other, this project contributes to strengthening peaceful conflict resolution and reconciliation at local levels.

The specific objective of this project is to strengthen&#xa0;social cohesion and civic trust within and between communities and between population and local government in five counties in Liberia. Community-based methodologies are implemented for strengthening peace, social cohesion and civic engagement as well as civic trust and enhancing good governance principles, including transparency, accountability, participation and inclusion.</narrative>
  </description>
